1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,528
Greasy streaks trapped between the panes
of your oven door?

2
00:00:03,889 --> 00:00:05,595
No cloth can reach them.

3
00:00:05,886 --> 00:00:08,556
But you can get inside the door safely,

4
00:00:08,615 --> 00:00:11,284
and make the glass crystal clear again.

5
00:00:12,434 --> 00:00:15,464
Seven steps, one screwdriver.

6
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:19,181
Stay for step six: the order of the

7
00:00:19,191 --> 00:00:21,234
panes really matters.

8
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:22,795
WikiTube.

9
00:00:23,086 --> 00:00:24,850
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:27,782
Most oven doors have two or three layers

11
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:30,789
of glass, and grease gets in through small

12
00:00:30,799 --> 00:00:32,145
vents at the top.

13
00:00:32,436 --> 00:00:34,946
To clean them, you remove the door and

14
00:00:34,956 --> 00:00:36,383
take the glass apart.

15
00:00:36,744 --> 00:00:38,740
It needs only a screwdriver.

16
00:00:39,286 --> 00:00:41,979
Designs vary, so check your manual.

17
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,963
If your door is sealed, with no screws,

18
00:00:45,022 --> 00:00:46,228
don't force it.

19
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:49,589
You'll need a screwdriver, dish soap and
warm

20
00:00:49,599 --> 00:00:53,711
water, microfiber cloths, a large towel to
protect

21
00:00:53,721 --> 00:00:56,483
the door, and your oven manual.

22
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,054
Step one.

23
00:00:58,345 --> 00:01:00,367
Turn the oven off and let it cool

24
00:01:00,377 --> 00:01:02,779
completely, for at least an hour.

25
00:01:03,744 --> 00:01:06,880
If you can, unplug it, or switch off

26
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:09,702
the power at the circuit breaker, and turn

27
00:01:09,712 --> 00:01:12,125
off the gas if you have a gas oven.

28
00:01:13,276 --> 00:01:15,553
Read the part of your manual that explains

29
00:01:15,563 --> 00:01:17,164
how to remove the door.

30
00:01:17,455 --> 00:01:19,907
Take photos of the door and hinges before

31
00:01:19,917 --> 00:01:23,851
you touch anything, so you remember how
everything fits.

32
00:01:24,398 --> 00:01:26,826
This is a job to do calmly and

33
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:27,961
with good light.

34
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:31,760
Also, remove any racks, so the oven is

35
00:01:31,770 --> 00:01:33,011
easier to reach.

36
00:01:33,372 --> 00:01:35,124
Let the lights cool, too.

37
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:36,839
Step two.

38
00:01:37,502 --> 00:01:40,011
Open the door fully, and look for the

39
00:01:40,021 --> 00:01:44,443
hinge locks, small metal clips or levers
on each hinge.

40
00:01:45,106 --> 00:01:47,859
Flip them to the locked position, as shown

41
00:01:47,869 --> 00:01:48,983
in your manual.

42
00:01:49,645 --> 00:01:52,491
Then close the door gently until it stops

43
00:01:52,501 --> 00:01:56,427
at about fifteen degrees, grip both sides,
and

44
00:01:56,437 --> 00:01:58,723
lift it up and out towards you.

45
00:01:59,386 --> 00:02:01,779
The door is heavier than it looks, so

46
00:02:01,789 --> 00:02:03,704
ask someone to help if needed.

47
00:02:04,669 --> 00:02:06,319
Lay it flat on a towel on a

48
00:02:06,329 --> 00:02:09,544
table or the floor, with the handle facing
you.

49
00:02:10,694 --> 00:02:13,099
If you can't find the locks, search the

50
00:02:13,109 --> 00:02:15,105
oven's model number online.

51
00:02:15,559 --> 00:02:18,681
A short video of your exact model can
help.

52
00:02:19,233 --> 00:02:20,231
Step three.

53
00:02:20,592 --> 00:02:22,553
Look at the top edge of the door,

54
00:02:22,914 --> 00:02:25,226
where there is usually a metal trim with

55
00:02:25,236 --> 00:02:28,555
two or three screws, or clips on the
sides.

56
00:02:29,706 --> 00:02:32,157
Remove the screws, and set them aside in

57
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:34,813
a cup, so they do not roll away.

58
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,425
Lift off the trim carefully.

59
00:02:38,227 --> 00:02:40,679
You will then see the inner glass panes,

60
00:02:40,689 --> 00:02:43,291
which slide out or lift out, held by

61
00:02:43,301 --> 00:02:45,401
small clips or rubber spacers.

62
00:02:45,948 --> 00:02:48,501
Keep track of the order of every part,

63
00:02:48,734 --> 00:02:50,521
taking a photo as you go.

64
00:02:51,323 --> 00:02:54,190
Tip the door gently to see if the trim
moves.

65
00:02:54,481 --> 00:02:57,234
Keep the door flat, so the glass doesn't

66
00:02:57,244 --> 00:02:58,811
slide out suddenly.

67
00:02:59,367 --> 00:03:00,411
Step four.

68
00:03:00,865 --> 00:03:03,859
Carefully slide out the middle pane or
panes,

69
00:03:03,953 --> 00:03:07,179
handling them by the edges, with both
hands.

70
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:11,359
Wear gloves, as glass edges can be sharp.

71
00:03:11,906 --> 00:03:14,554
Lay each pane on a clean towel, in

72
00:03:14,564 --> 00:03:18,104
order, and remember which side faced which
way.

73
00:03:19,255 --> 00:03:21,773
Some panes have a coating on one side,

74
00:03:21,797 --> 00:03:23,642
so note the orientation.

75
00:03:24,189 --> 00:03:27,868
If anything feels stuck, stop and check
your manual.

76
00:03:28,415 --> 00:03:29,981
Never force glass.

77
00:03:30,946 --> 00:03:33,627
If a pane is cracked, don't reuse it.

78
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,601
Place a soft cloth between the panes while

79
00:03:36,611 --> 00:03:39,214
they're stacked, if you must set them down

80
00:03:39,224 --> 00:03:42,102
together, so they don't scratch each
other.

81
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:43,734
Step five.

82
00:03:44,188 --> 00:03:46,372
Wash each pane in warm water with a

83
00:03:46,382 --> 00:03:49,414
little dish soap, using a soft sponge or

84
00:03:49,424 --> 00:03:50,967
a microfiber cloth.

85
00:03:52,118 --> 00:03:54,511
Burnt-on spots can be soaked with a paste

86
00:03:54,521 --> 00:03:57,469
of baking soda and water for fifteen
minutes,

87
00:03:57,493 --> 00:03:59,141
then gently wiped.

88
00:03:59,943 --> 00:04:03,393
Never use steel wool, scouring powders or
razor

89
00:04:03,403 --> 00:04:05,758
blades, which scratch the glass.

90
00:04:06,723 --> 00:04:09,894
Rinse well, then dry and polish each pane

91
00:04:09,904 --> 00:04:12,992
with a lint-free cloth until it's
streak-free.

92
00:04:13,538 --> 00:04:15,964
Clean the inside of the door frame too,

93
00:04:16,093 --> 00:04:18,042
and check the vents for grease.

94
00:04:18,496 --> 00:04:20,573
Take your time with the corners.

95
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:24,370
A thin, damp cloth wrapped around a ruler

96
00:04:24,463 --> 00:04:26,982
can help you reach narrow spots.

97
00:04:27,533 --> 00:04:28,681
Step six.

98
00:04:29,646 --> 00:04:31,783
Put the panes back in the reverse order

99
00:04:31,793 --> 00:04:34,590
that you took them out, using your photos.

100
00:04:35,392 --> 00:04:37,623
Make sure that each pane sits in its

101
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:41,361
slot or clip, with the same orientation,
and

102
00:04:41,371 --> 00:04:44,505
that any rubber spacers or gaskets are in
place.

103
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:47,433
Then put on the top trim, and tighten

104
00:04:47,443 --> 00:04:50,542
the screws gently, just until snug.

105
00:04:51,205 --> 00:04:53,503
Over-tightening can crack the glass.

106
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:55,618
Run your finger along the edge to make

107
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:59,076
sure everything is level, and wipe away
fingerprints.

108
00:04:59,436 --> 00:05:01,203
Take a final look through the glass in

109
00:05:01,213 --> 00:05:04,140
the light, since dust or smears are easy

110
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:06,831
to see before the door is closed up.

111
00:05:07,367 --> 00:05:08,585
Step seven.

112
00:05:09,248 --> 00:05:11,571
Hold the door at the same shallow angle

113
00:05:11,581 --> 00:05:14,474
as before, and slide the hinge arms back

114
00:05:14,484 --> 00:05:16,132
into the slots on the oven.

115
00:05:16,795 --> 00:05:19,501
Push the door fully down, then open it

116
00:05:19,511 --> 00:05:21,800
all the way and flip the hinge locks

117
00:05:21,810 --> 00:05:23,760
back to their normal positions.

118
00:05:24,724 --> 00:05:26,897
Close and open the door a few times

119
00:05:26,907 --> 00:05:30,122
to check that it moves smoothly and shuts
tightly.

120
00:05:31,086 --> 00:05:33,410
Switch the power back on, and run the

121
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:34,812
oven for a few minutes.

122
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:37,378
Check that the door seals properly.

123
00:05:37,739 --> 00:05:40,524
Take care to hold the door with both
hands.

124
00:05:41,187 --> 00:05:44,762
Once it is back, the oven should look like
new.

125
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,922
If the glass is still cloudy after
washing,

126
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:50,465
check each pane on both sides.

127
00:05:51,128 --> 00:05:54,415
Many doors have three layers, and the film

128
00:05:54,425 --> 00:05:56,758
can sit on a surface you skipped.

129
00:05:57,421 --> 00:06:00,046
A haze that survives a careful wash is

130
00:06:00,056 --> 00:06:03,471
usually etching, damage from years of
grease and

131
00:06:03,481 --> 00:06:06,963
strong cleaners, and it cannot be polished
away.

132
00:06:07,928 --> 00:06:10,809
In that case, order replacement glass from
the

133
00:06:10,819 --> 00:06:13,500
maker using your oven's model number.

134
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:16,587
Some situations call for a technician.

135
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:19,654
Hinge springs are under tension, so if the

136
00:06:19,664 --> 00:06:22,011
door will not release or snaps back when

137
00:06:22,021 --> 00:06:25,178
you remove it, stop and call.

138
00:06:26,328 --> 00:06:28,175
If you have a gas oven and smell

139
00:06:28,185 --> 00:06:31,124
gas at any point, leave the house, and

140
00:06:31,134 --> 00:06:34,326
call your gas emergency number from
outside.

141
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:37,347
Do not switch anything on or off, and

142
00:06:37,357 --> 00:06:39,586
stay out until it is safe.

143
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:43,093
A few habits keep grease from building up
again.

144
00:06:43,453 --> 00:06:45,893
Cover roasting dishes with a lid or loose

145
00:06:45,903 --> 00:06:49,466
foil, so fat does not spit onto the glass.

146
00:06:50,129 --> 00:06:52,046
Put a baking sheet on the lower rack

147
00:06:52,056 --> 00:06:53,321
to catch drips.

148
00:06:53,774 --> 00:06:55,912
Wipe the inside of the door after it

149
00:06:55,922 --> 00:06:59,161
has cooled, while spills are still soft.

150
00:06:59,614 --> 00:07:01,740
Do not rub the rubber seal around the

151
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:04,385
door, because cleaners can damage it.

152
00:07:04,933 --> 00:07:07,068
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

153
00:07:07,522 --> 00:07:11,909
First, rushing without reading your manual
or taking photos.

154
00:07:12,363 --> 00:07:14,672
If you can't remember how the parts fit,

155
00:07:14,848 --> 00:07:16,785
reassembly is hard.

156
00:07:17,587 --> 00:07:20,875
Second, using abrasive tools or razor
blades on

157
00:07:20,885 --> 00:07:25,005
the glass, which leave scratches that trap
grease.

158
00:07:25,366 --> 00:07:28,837
And third, forcing parts that don't want
to move.

159
00:07:29,197 --> 00:07:32,679
If something sticks, stop and check the
instructions,

160
00:07:32,704 --> 00:07:34,293
or ask a technician.

161
00:07:34,956 --> 00:07:38,740
Safety comes first with ovens, glass and
hinges.

162
00:07:39,403 --> 00:07:42,399
If anything feels unsafe, a technician can
do

163
00:07:42,409 --> 00:07:43,953
this job quickly.

164
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,590
Let's recap.

165
00:07:45,823 --> 00:07:48,086
Switch off the oven and let it cool.

166
00:07:48,749 --> 00:07:51,523
Remove the door, using the hinge locks.

167
00:07:51,884 --> 00:07:53,311
Open the top trim.

168
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:55,854
Slide out the glass panes.

169
00:07:56,818 --> 00:07:58,802
Wash and dry each pane.

170
00:07:59,767 --> 00:08:01,612
Reassemble in the same order.

171
00:08:02,066 --> 00:08:04,445
And refit the door and test it.

172
00:08:05,409 --> 00:08:08,801
Seven steps, about forty minutes, and an
oven

173
00:08:08,811 --> 00:08:10,714
door you can see through again.

174
00:08:11,679 --> 00:08:14,711
If the glass stays cloudy, replace it, and

175
00:08:14,721 --> 00:08:17,901
call a technician if anything feels
unsafe.

176
00:08:18,467 --> 00:08:20,942
That's how you clean between the glass on

177
00:08:20,952 --> 00:08:22,240
your oven door.

178
00:08:23,390 --> 00:08:26,189
If your oven window is clear again,
subscribe

179
00:08:26,199 --> 00:08:29,449
to WikiTube, because we publish a new
how-to

180
00:08:29,473 --> 00:08:30,900
every single day.

181
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,155
Tell us in the comments how greasy your

182
00:08:33,165 --> 00:08:35,257
oven was, and what you would like us

183
00:08:35,267 --> 00:08:36,578
to explain next.

184
00:08:37,031 --> 00:08:38,215
See you tomorrow.

185
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,529
That's WikiTube.

186
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:41,979
Whatever it is, here's how.
